 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "State liability",
   "texto": [
    "It is formed with **sein** + participle II: **Die Tür ist geschlossen** (the door is closed). It presents a state or result. With **werden** the process passive is formed: **Die Tür wird geschlossen** (it is closed / is being closed). This form does not force you to interpret that action happens right now: time and context complete the meaning. **Ist geschlossen** is not by itself a past time; it describes a state at the time of speech."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Process and outcome in context",
   "texto": [
    "**Der Patient wird operiert** presents the operation as a process or event; **Der Patient ist operiert** presents the patient as already operated. **Das Medikament wird eingenommen** may describe a general process or pattern; **Das Medikament ist eingenommen worden** expresses that someone took it. Not all participles naturally admit a state reading."
   ]
  },
